<http://data.silknow.org/object/1a89d4b0-7fe4-393a-9b39-b0f0fe47bb00/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "woven silk and metal thread bordered with two different woven silk and metal thread textiles, backed with plain weave cotton and faced with silk satin.\nThe central panel has a light blue satin ground with offset rows of a repeating motif in which two birds faced one another above a stem bearing 3 blossoms. Between the stems is a small vertical fish-like motif. All the motifs were worked in metal thread; the plants have green leaves and red details and the birds have red or white wings.  A square panel of this fabric forms the corners of the border.\nMetal Thread: silver strip open S-wound on a yellow silk core.\nThe sides and end borders are red silk satin with a small repeating motif of a stylized flower on the diagonal; each row slopes in the opposite direction. The motifs are worked in metal thread [silver strip open S-wound on a yellow silk core]. The upper border has been pieced.\nBacking: pieced; light pink cotton.\nFacing: bias cut; brownish-green satin."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/1a89d4b0-7fe4-393a-9b39-b0f0fe47bb00> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/1a89d4b0-7fe4-393a-9b39-b0f0fe47bb00/category/1>
