        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "woven silk, 1800s, Persian; Birds"@en , "woven silk and metal thread bordered with two different woven silk and metal thread textiles, backed with plain weave cotton and faced with silk satin.\nThe central panel has a light blue satin ground with offset rows of a repeating motif in which two birds faced one another above a stem bearing 3 blossoms. Between the stems is a small vertical fish-like motif. All the motifs were worked in metal thread; the plants have green leaves and red details and the birds have red or white wings.  A square panel of this fabric forms the corners of the border.\nMetal Thread: silver strip open S-wound on a yellow silk core.\nThe sides and end borders are red silk satin with a small repeating motif of a stylized flower on the diagonal; each row slopes in the opposite direction. The motifs are worked in metal thread [silver strip open S-wound on a yellow silk core]. The upper border has been pieced.\nBacking: pieced; light pink cotton.\nFacing: bias cut; brownish-green satin."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/3deb4d32-7fec-36b0-a81b-2265455ae732> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/5c41f4b9-c281-3744-adae-d572dd0a1ffa> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/f59c2871-3a98-3733-af19-ba78cd58ad60> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/71498043-10a5-3e26-98b2-c4ce7d7aba80> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "woven silk, 1800s, Persian; Birds"@en , "woven silk and metal thread bordered with two different woven silk and metal thread textiles, backed with plain weave cotton and faced with silk satin.\nThe central panel has a light blue satin ground with offset rows of a repeating motif in which two birds faced one another above a stem bearing 3 blossoms. Between the stems is a small vertical fish-like motif. All the motifs were worked in metal thread; the plants have green leaves and red details and the birds have red or white wings.  A square panel of this fabric forms the corners of the border.\nMetal Thread: silver strip open S-wound on a yellow silk core.\nThe sides and end borders are red silk satin with a small repeating motif of a stylized flower on the diagonal; each row slopes in the opposite direction. The motifs are worked in metal thread [silver strip open S-wound on a yellow silk core]. The upper border has been pieced.\nBacking: pieced; light pink cotton.\nFacing: bias cut; brownish-green satin."@en ;
